# The data stands before the code in every form of a launch (the author 2026-11-11,
# LMX_blog/2026-11-11.md#data-before-code): the former order `call: code data` is not read. Here the first argument
# holds the statement and the second the place, so the launch takes the holder of the statement as its data and the
# holder of the place as its code: that code declares x in data that has no x -- answer 3. Written `call: Data Code`
# the same launch gives Data\x = 2 (the fixture code_data).
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call
# main().
sub: main () (
    Code:
        x := x + 1
    Data:
        int: x 1
)
    call: Code Data
main()
int: seen main\data\Data\x
